# PART 16 — PRE-SPECIFY A PARSIMONIOUS PROPENSITY MODEL

Because the cohort is only approximately 147 patients with approximately 57 STRIDE patients, do NOT put dozens of sparse variables into an unrestricted ordinary logistic model.

Create a parsimonious clinically informed model prioritizing factors that plausibly influence BOTH treatment selection and prognosis.

Core candidate variables should include, if sufficiently complete:

1. baseline ALBI, continuous
2. age
3. sex
4. AFP, preferably transformed or clinically categorized
5. prior hepatic decompensation
6. portal hypertension / varices
7. recent major bleeding
8. anticoagulation
9. CKD / renal function
10. hypertension / vascular disease
11. autoimmune disease / immunosuppression
12. extrahepatic disease
13. macrovascular/portal vein invasion
14. prior liver-directed therapy
15. liver disease etiology
16. healthcare utilization proxy
17. site/provider group if appropriate

Do NOT include ECOG or Child-Pugh in the primary model because missingness is extreme.

Do NOT include post-index variables.

Avoid redundant variables in the same model.

For example:
- do not include baseline ALBI + albumin + bilirubin simultaneously unless there is a specific reason;
- do not include a composite portal-hypertension variable plus every component unless model size allows it.

